      "side": 1,
      "message": "Requesting 32 SGEs increases the provider’s SQ allocation. With `tx-queue-size 4096`, mlx5 allocates 65,536 WQEBBs. If hardware accepts that size, `min_log2(dv_qp.sq.wqe_cnt)` is 16, which truncates to zero in the four-bit `dv_sq_log2sz` field. Debug TX then asserts, while release TX uses incorrect ring masks. The non-TSO QP path has the same issue.\n\nCould we validate the returned SQ size against the field and counter limits, and adjust the allocation or representation accordingly?",
      "revId": "9742d1d65ef3f709792c8e9a8abbdd2350605ae2",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
