      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T14:19:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the fast loop has built a regular-send prefix, `last` initially points at the next unused WQE. If the first GSO packet returns `NO_SLOTS`, we signal that unused WQE instead of the prefix’s last WQE, so the prefix has no completion.\n\nFor example, 255 regular packets followed by GSO on an empty 256-slot buffer ring can leave subsequent TSO traffic unable to progress. Could we pass the prefix’s actual last WQE into this helper?",
      "revId": "9742d1d65ef3f709792c8e9a8abbdd2350605ae2",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    }
